DYNAMIC / SCOPE-BASED PERMISSIONS
=================================

These are intentionally kept separate from basic RBAC because the same
capability is constrained by ownership, target status, ticket type, or
special account assignment.


1. RESOURCE SCOPE: OWN
----------------------
Use resource-ownership authorization for the following capabilities:

contract.read.own
contract.regulation.read.own
contract.violation.read.own
invoice.read.own
receipt.read.own
premise.read.own.rented
contract.sign
contract.terminate
contract.cancel
premise.rent
premise.return
invoice.pay
contract.violation.pay
contract.violation.appeal

The policy must verify that the requested resource belongs to the
current customer/account where applicable.


2. CONTRACT STATUS TARGET
-------------------------
Use one permission:
contract.status.update

Do not create separate permissions for each target status.

Manager allowed targets:
- signed
- canceled
- terminated

Employee allowed targets:
- signed
- canceled

The target-status restriction belongs to authorization/business policy.


3. PREMISE STATUS TARGET
------------------------
Use one permission:
premise.status.update

Employee is allowed to change the premise status to:
- reserved

Additional target states should be controlled by policy instead of
creating one permission per status.


4. PREMISE DELETE BUSINESS RULE
------------------------------
The rule that a premise is hidden/cannot be soft-deleted when status is
"rented" is a business/authorization condition, not a separate role.


5. TICKET TYPE
--------------
Dynamic ticket-type policy:

Employee:
- violation ticket type: NOT allowed

Inspector:
- violation ticket type: allowed

Customer:
- violation ticket type: NOT allowed


6. SPECIAL EMPLOYEE PERMISSION
------------------------------
premise.media.update

This permission is intentionally NOT assigned to the Employee role by
default. Grant it through account_additional_permission to selected
employees.


7. CONTRACT CREATE / APPROVE SPECIAL RULES
-------------------------------------------
The source marks these permissions with "*":

contract.create *
contract.approve *

The exact meaning of "*" is not defined in the supplied requirements.
Keep them as normal permissions and implement the additional condition
in application authorization/business logic until that rule is defined.


MERGED / CONSOLIDATED AREAS
===========================

contract.status.update
    Manager: signed/canceled/terminated
    Employee: signed/canceled

contract.violation.read
    Manager/Inspector: read list
    Customer: contract.violation.read.own

receipt.read.list
    Shared by Manager and Employee.
    Customer uses receipt.read.own.

